ex at `n ≤ 32`","+(`G(n, 6/n)`, `G(n, 10/n)`, `(6, 1)` covers at `β*`; §4.6), and found the","+cluster around a planted pair to be two lobes of recombinations through the","+separator (§4.4–§4.5), typical on `G(n, c/n)` at about half the mean's","+rate and absent on covers (§4.7, the fork's middle branch and its artefact","+branch). This item writes the recombination count down as a `Z`, checks it,","+measures its lower tail on the same planted instances, writes the cleanest","+*computable* lower bound `Ẑ₀` whose transform is a finite sum of binomial","+probabilities, and gives the constant `β_W(c)` it yields. Per the item's","+(d), the rest of the session went to the near-threshold numbers at finer","+`c` (§9.6).","+","+**The events counted.** Three `Z` on the ordered exact-size empty pairs","+(`|A| = t`, `|R| = r = N − t`, `S = V ∖ (A ∪ R)`, `|S| = k`):","+","+* `Z_j(P) = 1 + #{recombinations of P with |U_A|, |U_R| ≤ j}` (§9.1; `j = 4`","+  measured, `Z_4`); `Z_all = Z_{j′} + Z_fl − 1` adds the flips of Lemma Fl","+  with `j′ = max(4, |L_A|, |L_R|)` so that `Ẑ₀ ≤ Z_all`;","+* `Ẑ₀(P) = C(|L_R| + t, t) + C(|L_A| + r, r) − 1`, with `L_A`, `L_R` the","+  separator vertices with no neighbour in `A`, in `R` (§9.3);","+* `X` itself (the ideal `Z`, `Y = 1[X > 0]`; §4.6).","+","+The item's `Z = 1 + max_j Z_j` is below the `1 + Σ_j` used here, which is","+admissible because the levels are distinguished by `|U_A|` (§9.1 (iii)).","+","+### 9.1 The recombination lemma (deterministic), and its check","+","+**Definition.** For an exact-size empty pair `P = (A, R)` with separator","+`S`, `d = t − r ∈ {0, 1}`, and `W_A, W_R ⊆ S` disjoint with no `W_A–W_R`","+edge, `U_A ⊆ A`, `U_R ⊆ R`:","+","+    same lobe:      A′ = (A ∖ U_A) ∪ W_A,  R′ = (R ∖ U_R) ∪ W_R,","+                    |U_A| = |W_A|, |U_R| = |W_R|, N_R(W_A) ⊆ U_R, N_A(W_R) ⊆ U_A;","+    reversed lobe:  A′ = (R ∖ U_R) ∪ W_A,  R′ = (A ∖ U_A) ∪ W_R,","+                    |W_A| = |U_R| + d, |W_R| = |U_A| − d, N_A(W_A) ⊆ U_A, N_R(W_R) ⊆ U_R.","+","+The separator vertices `W_A` join the `A′` side and `W_R` the `R′` side;","+their neighbours on the side they are joining against are *evicted* into","+the new separator (`U_A`, `U_R` must contain them), and the rest of `U_A`,","+`U_R` is drawn freely to keep the sizes. This is §4.5's mechanism, with","+§4.4's two lobes.","+","+**Lemma Rc.** (i) Every image `(A′, R′)` is an exact-size empty pair of","+`G`: `|A′| = t`, `|R′| = r` by the size conditions, and each of the four","+edge classes of `A′ × R′` is excluded — `(A ∖ U_A) × (R ∖ U_R)` by `P`","+empty, `W_A × (R ∖ U_R)` by `N_R(W_A) ⊆ U_R`, `(A ∖ U_A) × W_R` by","+`N_A(W_R) ⊆ U_A`, `W_A × W_R` by hypothesis (same lobe; the reversed lobe","+is the same four lines with the sides exchanged). (ii) On each lobe the","+map `(W_A, W_R, U_A, U_R) ↦ (A′, R′)` is injective: on the same lobe","+`U_A = A ∖ A′`, `W_A = A′ ∩ S`, `U_R = R ∖ R′`, `W_R = R′ ∩ S`; on the","+reversed lobe `U_R = R ∖ A′`, `W_A = A′ ∩ S`, `U_A = A ∖ R′`, `W_R = R′ ∩ S`.","+(iii) For `|U_A| < t`, the two lobes are disjoint (`A′ ∩ A = A ∖ U_A ≠ ∅`","+on the same lobe, `A′ ∩ A = ∅` on the reversed), the levels are","+distinguished by `|U_A|` and `|U_R|`, and the only image equal to `P` is","+the identity (same lobe, `W_A = W_R = ∅`). Hence","+`Z_j := 1 + #{images with |U_A|, |U_R| ≤ j < min(t, r)}` satisfies","+`1 ≤ Z_j ≤ X` on `{P empty}` and is admissible in Lemma W. ∎","+","+**Counting without enumerating `U`.** Given `(W_A, W_R)`, the admissible","+`(U_A, U_R)` are the supersets of the evicted neighbourhoods at the forced","+sizes, so on the same lobe the number of images is","+`C(t − |N_A(W_R)|, |U_A| − |N_A(W_R)|) · C(r − |N_R(W_A)|, |U_R| − |N_R(W_A)|)`","+(and with `N_A(W_A)`, `N_R(W_R)` on the reversed lobe); the families of","+`W` with a small evicted neighbourhood are closed under subsets, so a","+pruned depth-first search lists them exactly (`recombinations`;","+`recombination_pairs` lists the images themselves).","+","+**The check** (`09_lower_tail/check.log`; before the above was called a","+lemma): on **every labelled graph on 4, 5 and 6 vertices** (64 + 1,024 +","+32,768), at every width `k` with `min(t, r) ≥ 2`, for **every exact-size","+empty pair** (24 + 2,080 + 216,320 pairs), every image (24 + 5,760 +","+**1,345,280** recombined pairs) is in the enumerated set of exact-size","+empty pairs, has the forced sizes, is not `P`, the images are distinct, and","+the closed-form count equals the explicit enumeration; `Ẑ₀ ≤ Z ≤ X` on","+every pair; and Lemma W holds pointwise with `Z = Z_4` and `Z = Ẑ₀` on 300","+random `G(10, p)` at every width (2,100 `(graph, k)` pairs, `Y ≥ 1[X > 0]`","+and `Y(Ẑ₀) ≥ Y(Z_4)`). **Zero violations**, 3 s on 8 workers. The same","+check on 200 planted `G(16, 6/16)` instances is a test","+(`test_recombined_pairs_are_empty_on_planted_instances`).","+","+### 9.2 The measured lower tail on the planted instances","+","+Item 04's planted instances at `β*` (14 cells, 200 each, regenerated from","+their seeds by item 04's `planted_instance`; `X` read from `planted.csv`;","+`tail.csv`): `Z_4` with both lobes and its split, `Z_1 … Z_3`, the flip","+count `Z_fl`, `Ẑ₀`, `|L_A|`, `|L_R|`, and the order `Ẑ₀ ≤ Z_all ≤ X` on","+every instance (2,800 of 2,800; under a second of wall time on 8","+workers). The `β* + 0.1` cells are not a gain in the constant (§4.6) and","+were not run.","+","+| cell | `n` | `k` | `Z_4`: median | p10 | gm | share `Z_4 = 1` | same / rev lobe (median) | `Ẑ₀` median | share `Ẑ₀ = 1` (= `P₀` closed) | `Z_fl` median | `X` median | median `log Z_4 / log X` |","+|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|","+| `G(n, 6/n)` | 16 | 3 | 2 | 1 | 2.55 | 0.46 | 0 / 0 | 1 | 0.76 | 1 | 3 | 0.50 |","+| | 20 | 3 | 2 | 1 | 3.03 | 0.42 | 0 / 1 | 1 | 0.75 | 1 | 4 | 0.44 |","+| | 24 | 4 | 4 | 2 | 7.22 | 0.00 | 1 / 2 | 1 | 0.62 | 1 | 20 | 0.46 |","+| | 28 | 5 | 7.5 | 1 | 10.90 | 0.16 | 3.5 / 2 | 1 | 0.54 | 1 | 40 | 0.52 |","+| | 32 | 5 | 5.5 | 1 