42** | **0.017** | 0.010 | **0.018** | **0.010** | **0.012** | **0.005** | 0.19 | 0.55 | 0.35 | 0.14 |","+| `G(n, 10/n)` | 16 | 0.011 | 0.009 | 0.009 | 0.004 | 0.000 | 0.003 | 0.003 | 0.003 | 0.001 | 0.80 | 0.92 | 0.86 | 0.07 |","+| | 20 | 0.020 | 0.017 | 0.017 | 0.007 | 0.000 | 0.006 | 0.005 | 0.005 | 0.002 | 0.59 | 0.85 | 0.70 | 0.12 |","+| | 24 | 0.044 | 0.041 | 0.041 | 0.009 | 0.000 | 0.013 | 0.012 | 0.012 | 0.003 | 0.00 | 0.79 | 0.00 | 0.38 |","+| | 28 | 0.025 | 0.020 | 0.020 | 0.008 | 0.001 | 0.007 | 0.006 | 0.006 | 0.002 | 0.44 | 0.77 | 0.57 | 0.14 |","+| | 32 | **0.039** | **0.031** | **0.031** | **0.011** | 0.001 | **0.012** | **0.010** | **0.010** | **0.003** | 0.21 | 0.69 | 0.31 | 0.16 |","+| cover `(6, 1)` | 16 | 0.051 | 0.051 | 0.051 | 0.008 | 0.000 | 0.017 | 0.017 | 0.017 | 0.003 | 0.00 | 0.86 | 0.00 | 0.44 |","+| | 20 | 0.044 | 0.043 | 0.044 | 0.009 | 0.000 | 0.015 | 0.015 | 0.015 | 0.003 | 0.00 | 0.81 | 0.00 | 0.42 |","+| | 24 | 0.044 | 0.044 | 0.044 | 0.014 | 0.000 | 0.015 | 0.015 | 0.015 | 0.005 | 0.00 | 0.67 | 0.00 | 0.35 |","+| | 28 | **0.043** | **0.042** | **0.042** | **0.016** | 0.000 | **0.015** | **0.014** | **0.014** | **0.006** | 0.00 | 0.59 | 0.00 | 0.31 |","+","+Growth in `n` of the total slack `−log E[1/·]` (OLS over the sizes, nats","+per vertex): `G(n, 6/n)`: `X` `0.091 ± 0.020`, `Z_4` `0.047 ± 0.020`,","+`Z_all` `0.058 ± 0.019`, `Ẑ₀` `0.024 ± 0.004`; `G(n, 10/n)`: `0.060`,","+`0.048`, `0.048`, `0.016 ± 0.002`; covers: `0.034`, `0.031`, `0.031`,","+`0.029 ± 0.004`.","+","+What the tables say:","+","+1. **The recombinations are most of the measured union-bound slack at","+   these sizes, and the computable bound is a third of it.** At the largest","+   `n`, `Z_4` recovers 54% (`c = 6`), 79% (`c = 10`) and 98% (covers) of","+   `−log E[1/X]`; `Ẑ₀` recovers 26%, 28% and 37%. The flips (Lemma Fl)","+   are worth 0.000–0.010 nats per vertex and are inside `Z_all`. On","+   covers `Z_4` *is* the whole slack to two decimals: the cluster there is","+   the reversed pair and nothing else (§4.3), and `Z_4` contains it.","+2. **The lower tail of `Z_4` is `Z_4 = 1`, and `Z_4 = 1` lives inside the","+   closed pairs.** `Z_4 = 1` on 16–21% of the planted instances at `n =","+   28–32` where `N` is odd (0% where `N` is even, by the reversed pair), on","+   30–35% of the *closed* planted pairs, and never on an open one (every","+   `S` vertex avoiding a side is a level-0 move); `P(Z_4 = 1)` is 58%","+   (`c = 6`) and 56% (`c = 10`) of `E[1/Z_4]` at `n = 32`. So the","+   recombination count's transform is carried by the instances whose","+   planted pair is closed *and* has no two-sided move at `j ≤ 4`.","+3. **What `Z_4` has and `Ẑ₀` has not** is the two-sided moves (an `S`","+   vertex with one or two neighbours on the far side, evicted by a vertex","+   of `S` joining the other side) and the reversed lobe: on the median","+   planted instance at `n = 32`, `c = 6`, the same lobe holds 2 and the","+   reversed 2 recombinations beyond the identity, `Ẑ₀ = 1`. The price of","+   computability at `n = 32` is `0.018, 0.020, 0.026` nats per vertex","+   (`c = 6, 10`, covers) — `0.005, 0.007, 0.008` in `β`.","+4. **`log Z_4 / log X` is about a half on `G(n, c/n)` and one on","+   covers** (medians 0.43–0.52 at `c = 6`, 0.67–1.00 at `c = 10`): the","+   recombinations at `j ≤ 4` account for half the cluster's logarithm on","+   `G(n, 6/n)`, and the half they miss is at distance beyond four","+   evictions.","+","+### 9.3 The computable bound `Ẑ₀`, its transform, and `β_W(c)`","+","+**`Ẑ₀`.** Keep the same-lobe moves with one side's `W` empty: `W_R = ∅`","+forces `U_R = ∅`, hence `N_R(W_A) = ∅`, so `W_A` is any subset of","+`L_R = {w ∈ S : N_R(w) = ∅}` and `U_A` any `|W_A|`-subset of `A`;","+`Σ_i C(|L_R|, i) C(t, i) = C(|L_R| + t, t)` images with the identity, and","+symmetrically `C(|L_A| + r, r)`; the two families share the identity, so","+","+    Ẑ₀ = C(|L_R| + t, t) + C(|L_A| + r, r) − 1  ≤  Z_{max(|L_A|, |L_R|)}  ≤  X.","+","+Given `(A, R)`, the degrees `|N_A(w)|`, `|N_R(w)|` for `w ∈ S` are","+independent across `w` and across the two sides (disjoint edge sets, none","+of them an `A–R` edge), so `|L_A| ~ Bin(k, (1 − p)^t)` and `|L_R| ~ Bin(k,","+(1 − p)^r)` are independent under the planted law and","+","+    E[1/Ẑ₀ | P₀ empty] = Σ_{ℓ_A, ℓ_R = 0}^{k} Bin(k, (1−p)^t)(ℓ_A) · Bin(k, (1−p)^r)(ℓ_R) / (C(ℓ_R + t, t) + C(ℓ_A + r, r) − 1)","+","+(`z_hat_log_laplace`; checked against the average of `1/Ẑ₀` over every","+planted graph at `n = 6`, `test_z_hat_laplace_against_the_planted_enumeration`;","+the resulting bound `E[X] · E[1/Ẑ₀]` is above `P(pw ≤ k)` on every labelled","+graph at `n = 5` and below the pair count,","+`test_weighted_bound_is_valid_on_every_labelled_graph_at_five`).","+","+**`Ẑ₀ = 1` iff `P₀` is closed.** `|L_A| = |L_R| = 0` says every separator","+vertex sees both sides, i.e. `S = N(A) ∩ N(R)` (L2). So","+`E[1/Ẑ₀ | P₀ empty] ≥ P(P₀ closed | P₀ empty) = (q_t q_r)^k`, and the","+weighted count with `Ẑ₀` is at least the closed-pair count at the forced","+sizes (the corner term of Theorem Cl): **`β_W ≤ β_closed` for this `Ẑ₀`**,","+exactly. The question is how much below.","+","+**The exponent.** With `a = (1 − β)/2`, `π = e^{−ca}` and `λ_A, λ_R` the","+fractions of `n` in `L_A`, `L_R`,","+","+    (1/n) log E[1/Ẑ₀]  →  − inf_{λ_A, λ_R ∈ [0, β]} [ β KL(λ_A/β ‖ π) + β KL(λ_R/β ‖ π) + max( (λ_R + a) H(λ_R/(λ_R + a)), (λ_A + a) H(λ_A/(λ_A + a)) ) ]","+","+(`z_hat_exponent`; the entropy terms are `(1/n) log C(λ n + a n, a n)`).","+At `λ = 0` the bracket is `2β(−ln q(a))`, the closed count's gain (§6.1","+(b)); the derivative along `λ_A = λ_R = λ → 0` is `2 ln(λ/(βπ)) − ln(λ/a) +","+O(1) → −∞`, so the minimiser is interior but at `λ = 0.0006`, and the value","+is `0.0006` nats below the corner (`laplace.csv`, `beta_w.csv`):","+","+| `c` | `β*` | `β_closed` | **`β_W`** | `β_W − β_closed` | `β_sep` (fitted) | gain of `β_W` over `β*` | in nats at `β*` | `2β ln q(a)` | minimiser `λ` |","+|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|","+| 3 | 0.0087 | 0.0096 | 0.0096 | +0.0000 | 0.0374 | +0.0009 | 0.0044 | −0.0044 | 0.00001 |","+| 4 | 0.0613 | 0.0671 | 0.0671 | −0.0001 | 0.0833 | +0.0058 | 0.0201 | −0.0204 | 0.0003 |","+| 6 | 0.1706 | 0.1803 | **0.1801** | **−0.0002** | 0.1820 | +0.0095 | 0.0290 | −0.0296 | 0.0006 |","+| 8 | 0.2628 | 0.2722 | 0.2720 | −0.0002 | 0.2691 | +0.0092 | 0.0277 | −0.0283 | 0.0006 |","+| 10 | 0.3371 | 0.3453 | **0.3451** | **−0.0002** | 0.3410 | +0.0080 | 0.0245 | −0.0250 | 0.0005 |","+| 12 | 0.3973 | 0.4043 | 0.4041 | −0.0001 | 0.3999 | +0.0068 | 0.0213 | −0.0217 | 0.0004 |","+| 16 | 0.4882 | 0.4933 | 0.4932 | −0.0001 | 0.4895 | +0.0050 | 0.0161 | −0.0164 | 0.0003 |","+| 20 | 0.5535 | 0.5573 | 0.5572 | −0.0001 | 0.5543 | +0.0037 | 0.0126 | −0.0128 | 0.0002 |","+","+The finite transform converges to the exponent from above","+(`laplace.csv`, `G(n, 6/n)` at `β*`): `(1/n) log E[1/Ẑ₀] = −0.018, −0.025,","+−0.027, −0.028, −0.029, −0.029, −0.029, −0.0291` at `n = 32, 64, 128, 256,","+512, 1024, 2048, 3200` against the asymptotic `−0.0290`, and `log P(P₀","+closed)` beside it within `0.001` per vertex at every `n`; at `c = 10`:","+`−0.013 → −0.0245` against `−0.0245`. At `n = 32` the transform","+(`−0.0182`, `−0.0126` per vertex) reproduces the planted measurement of","+§9.2 (`0.017`, `0.011`) to the sampling error. **The typical `Ẑ₀` is","+exponentially large** — `|L| ≈ β e^{−ca} n = 0.014 n` vertices avoid a","+side, giving `log Ẑ₀ ≈ 0.06 n` at `c = 6` and `0.05 n` at `c = 10` — and","+none of it reaches the constant: the transform is the lower tail.","+","+**Why no level-`j` `Ẑ` with a clean transform does better.** A one-sided","+level-1 family (reversed lobe, `N` odd, `W_R = ∅`, so `|N_A(W_A)| ≤ 1`)","+has the vertices with exactly one `A`-neighbour entering *linearly* — only","+the degree-zero vertices combine freely — so its transform is the","+one-sided level-0 tail `β(−ln q)`, worse than `Ẑ₀`'s two-sided one. A",